Finally won the damn thing on a UNIX system, although I'd gone through
the motions on wizard mode on a PC.

I won with a priest, no polypile, no shop credit bug.  I found a WOW in
a chest on the graveyard/temple to Nalzok.

Possible spoilers.


Comments:

I like some parts of the game like the new hell levels with ascending
and descending stairwells.  However, I wasted a whole hour getting 
screwed around the wizard levels ascending with the amulet.  It's
EXTREMELY annoying to get randomly teleported into a no-dig area of
the wizard's top level and have to go back down several levels and
repeat the whole process.  I was lucky to have a cursed gain level
potion to get up through the stupid room.

I don't like the last level with all the angels of every denomination
beating the hell out of you.  I had a -28 AC with ~700 hps and I was
down to 300 when I ascended.  I ascended "extremely unlucky" due to
killing all those stupid angels.

I also hate the air elemental plane.  That place is tougher than any
in hell.  Not as tough as the ascension level, but it was very painful.
And it took me a while to figure out what the hell "Kaboom!  Boom! Boom!
Kaboom!  You can move again." meant...

TIPS

Always attempt to leave a crystal ball in your bag of holding or near
the top stairs ready for use.  You'll need them for detecting the portal
on the elemental planes.  I was stupid and didn't get one, and I was 
lucky to get one from killing a dragon on the plane of air.  Use the
'/' or ';' to check among the fire traps for the true portal.

Try to clear out paths in hell for a quick escape BEFORE killing the
Wizard.  Otherwise he'll curse your pick axe and you'll be pissed.

Fight demon lords with your Vorpal Blade, because they will otherwise
attempt to heal themselves.

Save a wish or two for a cockatrice corpse in case you're having problems
with the Wiz or some other nasty creatures.  I was stupid (again) and used
my wish before getting the blessed scroll of charging.  augh.

Break up your piles of stuff that you use often (food rations, holy water)
in your bag of holding, since pulling out 17 food rations may suddenly
slow you down just while you're attempting to get out of a "fainting"
situation.

Grab all potions in hell you can and convert them to water and then to
holy water.  You'll need them for the wonderful things that the Wizard
does to you after you kill his ass.

Carry all the create monster wands with you that you can to the temple of
whatever (as a priest), and zap 'em a billion times to get loads more
wraiths than you deserve.  Can giant flesh for strength.  Save and
snack on royal jelly too if you can get it.

Leaving your bag of holding on the floor in water levels will allow all
stuff to be erased.  Carry the bag with you at all times if possible or
leave it on a dry level and come back and get it later.

If you don't want monsters to get at stuff lying around, put it in a
chest and lock it up.

Whomever thought of the engraving with gems to ID them bit, that is a
stroke of brilliance.  I won with loads of valuable gems piled into
the bag of holding, and that gave me tons of points.  To do it, simply
attempt to engrave with the gem.  If it says "You attempt to engrave
your message...", then #name 'n' 'y' the object to VALUABLE [color].
If the message says 'You write in the dust with your ...', then name
it 'soft [color]' and identify them later in order not to miss the
softer gems.

Resist the temptation to carry non-rustproof weapons with you to hell.
They WILL rust, and you will be pissed.

Anyway, that's all I can think of now.

